umni Association Board Of Directors Alumni Sponsored Awards & Scholarships Endowed Scholarships Alumna and Alumnus of the Year Campus Spirit Award The Sarah M Laven Purpose Road Endowed Scholarship Class of 1982 Student Teacher Award Alumni Groups & Organizations Voices Of Appalachia The Gatton Winston Scholars Program Update Your Alumni Profile Share Your Story Ways To Give Back: Alumni Appalachia Day Homecoming A Legacy Of Service About About Overview Contact Us College Profile Our Mission Our Values The Purpose Road Our Service Area Accreditation Student Achievement Visit Alice Lloyd College News History of Alice Lloyd College The June Buchanan School June Buchanan School Homepage The June Buchanan School Application JBS School Calendar JBS Extracurricular Activities JBS Faculty and Staff Support JBS Contact Us Alice Lloyd College Career Services Home » Career Services Student Life Helping You Build a Career You're Proud Of Career Services helps Alice Lloyd College students and alumni explore career paths, build job search skills, and connect with employers. Whether you’re choosing a major, applying for internships, or preparing for life after graduation, we’re here to help — ideally starting as early as your sophomore year. Your 4-Year Roadmap Career Success Plan Freshman Year Explore majors, build foundational skills, and start thinking about your path. Take a skills assessment to discover your strengths and interests Attend a career exploration workshop or seminar Get involved in clubs or activities that build real, transferable skills Undecided on a major? Talk with an advisor — we’ll help you figure it out Sophomore Year Confirm your direction and make your first real career connections. Meet with a career counselor to lock in (or rethink) your major Attend a job fair to see what’s out there Set up a shadowing day or informational interview with an alum Considering grad school? Start researching programs early and look into entrance exam requirements, since some can take months to prepare for Junior Year Gain real experience and start building your professional network. Land an internship, co-op, or part-time job in your field Get your resume reviewed by a career counselor — before you need it Start networking with alumni and professionals now, not later Considering grad school? Research programs and register for entrance exams Senior Year Turn your plan into a job offer — or your next degree. Polish your resume and register for career fairs Practice your interview skills before the real thing; practice truly helps Build a job search plan with Career Services Lock in your references, and don’t forget to request your free copy of Job Choices — a handy guide to the job market nationwide KEEP LOOKING Helpful Job Search Resources USAJobs.gov — Search federal government job openings CareerOneStop — U.S. Department of Labor career exploration tools O*NET Online — Explore careers and see detailed job descriptions, skills, and requirements Occupational Outlook Handbook — U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics career profiles, including pay and job outlook NACE Salary Calculator Center — Estimate salaries by job title, location, and experience LinkedIn Jobs — Search jobs and build your professional network Kentucky Nonprofit Network — Nonprofit job openings across Kentucky Always Here When You Need Us Visit or Contact Career Services Office Hours: Monday–Friday, 8:00 a.m.–4:30 p.m. Evenings by appointment Staff: Nathan Hall, Career Services Director Location: 2nd Floor, Jerry C. Davis Student Center, Room 208 Contact: Alice Lloyd College Career Service Office 100 Purpose Rd, Pippa Passes, KY 41844 Phone: (606) 368-6136 Email: [email protected] Help Prepare the Next Generation of Appalachian Leaders Alice Lloyd College is a 501(c)(3) tax-exempt organization. EIN: 61-0492351. Give The Gift of Tuition Alice Lloyd College Alice Lloyd College is a private, Christian Work College located in Pippa Passes, Kentucky, committed to providing accessible, purpose-driven education for students across Appalachia. Facebook-f Instagram Youtube Tiktok Quick Links About Alice Lloyd College June Buchanan School News Schedule a Visit How to Apply Our Service Area Our Values About Alice Lloyd College June Buchanan School News Schedule a Visit How to Apply Our Service Area Our Values Visit Us 100 Purpose Rd, Pippa Passes, KY 41844 (606) 368-6000 Designed By Forcht Media Copyright © 2026 All rights reserved."
